body:
In commit [bdc489b38d0fa9b76f60d3e54de16c975262d72e](https://github.com/microsoft/vscode/commit/bdc489b38d0fa9b76f60d3e54de16c975262d72e), the following code:

```ts
// Merge contents of the identifier only at the end to take precedence.
mergeContents(contentsForIdentifierOnly);
```

causes this configuration:

```jsonc
"[markdown][mdx]": {
    "editor.wordWrap": "wordWrapColumn",
}
```

to **not** override the default settings for `markdown`. Only this works:

```jsonc
"[markdown]": {
    "editor.wordWrap": "wordWrapColumn",
}
```

**My question:** What is the design rationale behind giving single-identifier overrides the highest precedence? I am considering making a change to this behavior and would like to understand the reasoning before proceeding.
